 ## 7. Score outputs
 
+`dope_kpi real-ref --arena DIR --schedule FILE --out realref.jsonl` writes one
+object per (cell, auditor), sorted by (`cell_id`, `auditor`): `cell_id`,
+`cell_sha256` (SHA-256 of the canonical schedule line; `score` refuses a
+reference computed from another schedule), `auditor`, `status` (`ok` or
+`unsupported`), `reason`, `num_outputs`, `informative`, `informative_reason`,
+`l0`, `l_a`, `l_b`, `r_b`, `real_gain_lcb95`, `c2st_real_ref`, and per T row
+`y_true`, `null_losses`, `real_a_losses`, `real_b_losses`, `pred_a`, `pred_b`.
+`informative` is the contract rule as computed by `dvs::v3::harm::assess_parity`
+on real losses only (real gain >= 1% of the null loss, bootstrap LCB95 > 0,
+twin retention within [0.8, 1.2]); the bootstrap seed is the stream
+`informative|<view>|<auditor>`. A cell is `unsupported` for every arm when its
+schedule status is `unsupported`, a real target is invalid, the A target is
+constant, the T target is constant, or the view exceeds an auditor's limits
+(1024 columns; 2,000,000 cells for the neural recipes).
+
 `dope_kpi score` writes, per arm:
 
 - `ledger.jsonl`: `dope_core::dvs::v3::FidelityCellRequest` objects (one per
-  cell x auditor x sample seed x multiplier), sorted by `cell_id`, reducible by
-  `evaluate_v3`.
-- `rows.jsonl`: one compact object per ledger entry: `cell_id`, `family_id`,
-  `task`, `view`, `stratum`, `auditor`, `data_seed`, `sample_seed`,
-  `multiplier`, `l0`, `l_a`, `l_b`, `l_s`, `r_s`, `r_b`, `informative`,
-  `status`, `packet_bytes`, `artifact_class`, `c2st_auc`, `c2st_real_ref`.
-
+  cell x auditor x sample seed x multiplier), reducible by `evaluate_v3`. The
+  existing ledger reader refuses a repeated `cell_id`, so the entry id is
+  `<cell_id>:s<sample_seed>:m<multiplier>:<auditor>` and the file is sorted by
+  that id. A missing log row or file, a malformed or mis-shaped file and a
+  failed auditor are `failed` entries, never skips.
+- `rows.jsonl`: one compact object per ledger entry, in the same order:
+  `cell_id`, `family_id`, `task`, `view`, `stratum`, `auditor`, `data_seed`,
+  `sample_seed`, `multiplier`, `l0`, `l_a`, `l_b`, `l_s`, `r_s`, `r_b`,
+  `informative`, `status` (`ok`, `failed`, `over_budget`, `unsupported`),
+  `packet_bytes`, `artifact_class`, `c2st_auc`, `c2st_real_ref`, plus `rows`
+  (synthetic rows read), `reason` (empty when `ok`) and `ledger_id`. `r_s` is
+  null when the real gain `l0 - l_a` is not positive.
+
+Unit space: features are standardised with the mean and standard deviation of
+the cell's A rows (a constant column is centred only) and a missing cell takes
+the A median; a regression target is standardised with the A target
+statistics. The same transform is applied to B, C, T and every synthetic table.
 Losses: mean squared error in A-standardised target units for regression,
 log-loss (probabilities clipped at 1e-12 and renormalised) for classification.
+The null predictor is the A mean or the A class prior.
+
+Auditors: `linear-seeded-v1`, `gbdt`, `mlp-seeded-v1` with the recipes of
+`dope_core::eval` and one seed per cell (stream `auditor`) shared by the A, B
+and synthetic fits. Count-based knobs scale with `rows / len(a_idx)` (at least
+1): gbdt `min_leaf` and `lambda`, and the batch of the neural recipes. With
+this, a table that repeats every row `k` times yields the model of the
+unrepeated table; the unscaled recipes do not.
+
+Realism: `dvs::v3::c2st::build_native_realism_input` with the cell's B rows as
+real and the synthetic rows as synthetic (the first `min(n_B, n_S)` of each,
+features and target in unit space). `c2st_real_ref` is the same test with the
+A rows in place of the synthetic rows. Privacy: A, B and synthetic rows in unit
+space rounded to 6 decimals, at most `--privacy-rows` of each (default 4096;
+0 writes no privacy input). `driver` and `deploy_roster` are absent, so a
+strict `evaluate_v3` fails every cell on the driver gate; `dope_kpi
+reduce-ledger --allow-partial` reduces without it, with `--kappa-file` for the
+thresholds and `--multiplier` / `--auditors` to select entries.
